{"name":"At Ease Soldier","hex":"#9e9985","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ease","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Lack of difficulty; the ability to do something easily.","Comfort, a state or quality lacking unpleasantness, particularly:"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To free (something) from pain, worry, agitation, etc.","To alleviate, assuage or lessen (pain)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ease"},{"term":"soldier","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of a ground-based army, of any rank, but especially an enlisted member.","Any member of a military, regardless of specialty."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To continue steadfast; to keep striving.","To serve as a soldier."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soldier"}],"entries":[{"title":"At Ease","blocks":[{"text":"At Ease was an alternative to the Macintosh desktop developed by Apple Computer in the early 1990s for the classic Mac OS. It provided a simple environment for new Macintosh users and young children to help them to work without supervision. At Ease replaces the Finder desktop, providing a simple tabbed panel-oriented graphical user interface in which applications and documents are represented by icons on large buttons. Aside from its security features, its interface and basic functionality is very similar to the Packard Bell Navigator."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/62/Ateaseuserfolder.png/330px-Ateaseuserfolder.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/At_Ease","wikidata":"Q4812304"},{"title":"Soldier","blocks":[{"text":"A soldier is a person who is a member of an army. A soldier can be a conscripted or volunteer enlisted person, a non-commissioned officer, a warrant officer, or an officer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/2ID_Recon_Baghdad.jpg/330px-2ID_Recon_Baghdad.jpg?utm_so